	(text "Formula: C1 ≥ 4 × C2,   Z0 = √(L_cable / C2)   \nData: L_cable = 1 µH, C2 = 4.7 µF, V_TVS(clamp) = 29.2 V\nResolution: C1 ≥ 4 × 4.7 µF = 19 µF\n              Z0 = sqrt(1 µH / 4.7 µF) ≈ 0.46 Ω  → target ESR\nChosen: 100 µF (standard value), rated 50 V "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.514 80.264 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "cff2c0ea-d54c-4446-9872-d4052c664e15")
	)
	(text "The chosen switching frequency is 2 MHz: it is below the maximum frequency allowed\nby the buck converter and above the AM radio band.\n\nThe inductor was chosen according to the datasheet reference design (4.7 µH).\n\nFORMULA:\nripple = V_OUT / (L × f_SW) × (1 − V_OUT / V_IN(MAX))   (datasheet p. 14)\nCapacitor charging: I_C = C × V / t\nI_PEAK = I_C + I_LOAD + ripple / 2\n\nDATA:\nV_OUT = 5 V\nV_IN(MAX) = 17 V\nL = 4.7 µH\nf_SW = 2 MHz\nC = 130 µF (total capacitance on the 5 V rail)\nt = 3.9 ms (soft-start time, datasheet p. 16)\nI_LOAD = 45 mA\n\nRESOLUTION:\nripple = 5 V / (4.7 µH × 2 MHz) × (1 − 5 V / 17 V)\n       = 0.53 A × 0.71\n       ≈ 0.38 A\n\nI_C = 130 µF × 5 V / 3.9 ms\n    ≈ 0.17 A\n\nI_PEAK = 0.17 A + 0.045 A + 0.38 A / 2\n       = 0.17 A + 0.045 A + 0.19 A\n       ≈ 0.40 A\n\nCHOSEN:\nInductor 4.7 µH, shielded, AEC-Q200, with I_SAT ≥ 1 A\n(more than twice the 0.40 A peak).\n\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 132.588 116.078 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e337f08c-4851-4740-8747-92aab8df3724")
	)
